{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"omphacite-emigratory-firecrest","creation_channel":"python","description":"# J1 — Freeze the Cloud adapter's behavior with characterization oracles before anything moves\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe DC work requires moving shared units out of `adapters/jira/`, and the Cloud adapter is the battle-tested\npath validated against a live Jira tenant. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_characterization.py`\nexists as the held-out Jira oracle, but it was not written to pin the specific outputs of the units about to\nmove, and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_contract.py` asserts only the vendor-neutral port contract\n(\"nothing satisfied by hard-coding Jira outputs\", per its own docstring). So today a silent mapping change\nduring extraction could pass CI.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend the characterization suite until it pins, by exact expected value, the current output of every unit that\nthe next story moves:\n\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` — `_map_local_to_jira_fields` for a representative ticket, plus\n  `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_STATUS` / `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_PRIORITY` for every key AND the default-fallback value.\n- `adapters/jira/jira_fields.py` — `_sanitize_label` / `_sanitize_summary` / `_sanitize_comment` at, below, and\n  above their limits, plus the invalid-label raise.\n- `adapters/jira/comment_limits.py` — `truncate_comment_body` at and above the limit.\n- `adapters/jira/identity.py` — `JiraIdentityConvention` format/parse/predicate, including the legacy\n  `rebar-id-` hyphen form.\n- `adapters/jira/probe.py` — `classify_probe_response` for each status code it branches on.\n- `adapters/jira/backend.py:42-72` — `map_fields_to_remote` for each of its branches.\n- `link_direction.resolve_inbound_link` + `jira_fields._RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK` for every relation.\n\nThese are golden-value assertions deliberately, not behavioral abstractions: their whole job is to fail if a\nbyte of output changes during a move that is supposed to change nothing.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** relying on the existing contract suite. It is explicitly written to be\nbackend-agnostic, so it cannot detect a Jira-specific mapping regression — that is what makes it a good contract\nsuite and a useless extraction oracle.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_characterization.py` — extended.\n- No `src/` change whatsoever in this story.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier against the real functions (no doubles): these are pure mappers and sanitizers, so the smallest tier\nthat crosses the mechanism is a direct call, and the oracle is the exact returned value.\n\n- happy path: each unit's output equals a literal expected value recorded in the test.\n- edge: every value map is asserted for all keys AND for an unmapped key hitting the documented default\n  (`\"To Do\"` / `\"Medium\"`), since the default is the branch an extraction is most likely to drop.\n- failure path: `_sanitize_label` still raises on an unfixable label, and `classify_probe_response` still\n  classifies its error statuses.\n- mutation check: for at least three pinned units, temporarily alter the source value (e.g. change a status-map\n  entry) and record that the characterization test goes RED — proving the oracle actually gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] every symbol listed in the Approach section has at least one exact-value assertion in\n      `test_backend_characterization.py`\n- [ ] `make test` passes with no `src/` modification in this change\n- [ ] [operator-attested] for three pinned units, altering the source value makes the corresponding\n      characterization test FAIL — the pytest failure output for each of the three is pasted into a\n      ticket comment, naming the unit and the value altered\n- [ ] a coverage check shows every branch of `map_fields_to_remote` and `classify_probe_response` is exercised","id":"daa2-789e-df12-4d9b","parent_id":"6c34-2d41-5f22-42a6","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"J1 — freeze the Cloud adapter's behavior with characterization oracles before anything moves"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788233758265864001,"uuid":"ea2a5b25-2fb8-43ca-b5e9-2078810371f0"}